### Guard the cache directory before creating it

**Severity:** `high`

`Path.GetDirectoryName(cacheFilePath)` is nullable, but its result is passed directly to `Directory.CreateDirectory`, which fails the current build under nullable analysis. Return `false` when the cache path has no directory component, then create the directory only after that guard. This preserves the method's existing failure contract and prevents an invalid cache path from escaping its error handling.

```suggestion
                var directory = Path.GetDirectoryName(cacheFilePath);
                if (directory is null)
                {
                    return false;
                }

                Directory.CreateDirectory(directory);
```
